{{!
Copy of the swagger-codegen-generators JavaSpring (handlebars) pojo template with two changes:
 - toString() renders on a single line instead of the default multi-line form;
 - the @NotUndefined marker is dropped, so that no io.swagger.configuration support classes
   and no jackson-databind-nullable dependency are needed (see model.mustache).

Branches that the generator options in build.gradle can never reach are stripped, so this
template only renders what it actually emits. It assumes useOas2=false and jackson=true (the
codegen default), and that gson, withXml, serializableModel and notNullJacksonAnnotation stay
unset. That drops the OAS2 @ApiModel/@ApiModelProperty variants, the Gson @SerializedName
markers, the Jackson/JAXB XML annotations and the Serializable boilerplate. The
useBeanValidation branches are deliberately left in place: unlike the ones above they pick
between two partials mid-line, so collapsing them would change the emitted whitespace.
Changing any of those options means restoring the matching branch from upstream.
Original template is here:
https://github.com/swagger-api/swagger-codegen-generators/blob/master/src/main/resources/handlebars/JavaSpring/pojo.mustache
}}
